course: dictionary
lesson: 8043
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning you need. The word register is a good example. «The register is taken every day» means the teacher checks the names on an official list, because a register is a list.
explain: To register can mean to put your name on an official list. «Metal rivets were patented (registered as an invention) in 1873» means they were officially recorded. To register can also mean to notice something: «it didn't register» means it did not sink in.
explain: Register can also mean how formal your words are. «Formal» language is careful and polite, for teachers and official letters; «informal» language is relaxed, for friends and family. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap it in to check it still makes sense.
fact: A register is an official list of names or things, such as the class list a teacher takes each morning.
fact: To register means to put your name on an official list, for example for a club or to vote.
fact: A cash register is the machine in a shop that holds the money and adds up prices.
fact: To register can also mean to notice or understand something, as in «it didn't register», or for a machine to show a number.
fact: Your register is how formal or informal your words are: «formal language for governors, chattier words for friends».
exercise: «The register is taken every day, so every name is checked.» What is a register here? | A type of cold weather | A quick way to walk | A loud noise in the hall | *An official list of names
exercise: Rivets were «registered as an invention» in 1873. What does registered mean here? | *Officially recorded | Stolen from a shop | Lost in a drawer | Painted bright red
exercise: In a shop, what does a cash register do? | Takes the register at school | Tells the time | *Holds the money and adds up prices | Warms the water in the pipes
test: Dina says, «It didn't register with me.» What does register mean? | *Did not notice or understand it | Did not sign the list | Did not pay for the item | Did not hear the bell
test: Ali writes a letter to the head teacher using careful, polite words. What is this style called? | Cash register | *Formal register | Informal register | Shop register
exam: The teacher says, «Let's take the register.» What does register mean? | A way of walking slowly | *An official list of names | A loud bell that starts the lesson | A cold dinner in the hall
